    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 6.00 no-show fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 4.80 of it.\n\nThe fee is chargeable under POL-NS-01 only if all four limbs hold, and each does. (a) The trip record (EV-TRIP-00202) carries a driver 'arrived' event at 23:13:10. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00202) places the driver inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius from the first qualifying fix at 23:12:45 — 25 seconds before the marker — with 63 qualifying in-radius fixes and a closest approach of about 22 m, so the POL-NS-02 proximity test is met on admissible fixes, and the zone class is taken from the trip record, not assumed. (c) The driver held position continuously for 620 seconds (23:12:45 to 23:23:05), 140 seconds more than the 480-second AIRPORT minimum, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as the clause requires and not from the arrived tap. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 23:23:20 on RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the minimum elapsed, with no boarding event.\n\nNo rider-exonerating clause applies. POL-NS-06 has no shortfall to bite on — the dwell exceeds the minimum. POL-NS-05 does not fire: at the marker the driver was stationary roughly 22 m from the pin, neither over 300 m away nor moving at 15 km/h or above. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver was inside the arrival radius rather than outside it. POL-NS-04 fails at its limb (a): the chat log holds no rider message at all — a SYSTEM arrival notice at 23:13:11 and two driver messages at 23:14:02 and 23:19:30 — so the rider-contact route is closed before limb (c) is ever reached. The rider's account of a delayed flight and of being in the terminal is not a limb of the charge and does not displace the arithmetic: POL-NS-06 fixes the fee on the driver's dwell 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages', and POL-NS-01 contains no rider-presence limb. The rider's position (device stationary 2.0 to 2.2 km from the pin, zero qualifying fixes inside the 200 m presence radius) is therefore not used against the rider, and equally does not defeat the charge.\n\nThe fee reconciles with fee_schedule: the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 6.00, exactly the fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee line, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. The trace and chat are unimpaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (c): 116 fixes at a 10 s cadence with no gaps (max gap 0 s, 100% coverage), no clock skew approaching 90 seconds, and three chat messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 3. EV-ADVIS-00202-01 (traffic advisory) is MISSING and carries weight 0.0, but it carries no deciding fact — only a single in-geofence interval exists, so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is not in play, and nothing in this ruling rests on it, so it does not cap confidence.\n\nPOL-NS-07 then applies. With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the SGD 6.00 fee = SGD 4.80, the residual 20 percent retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming guard does not trip: driver no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1 of 168 completed trips in 30 days is far below the 0.08 rate, so neither limb is met and no escalation arises. Per POL-GEN-03, on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd; the filing party's own charge is unaffected. The rider's profile counters (prior_no_show_flags, rating, lifetime_trips, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld) and the driver's rating and acceptance_rate are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground no finding against either party. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
